t-id status="new" format="epo"><country>EP</country><doc-number>0240867</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-5224420-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>5224420</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1114818A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit> </non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOUSAKA HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country> </address> </addressbook> </applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA YASUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISSAN CHEMICAL IND LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOUSAKA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA, YASUYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISSAN CHEMICAL INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOUSAKA HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA YASUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOUSAKA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA, YASUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process which enables easy and inexpensive preparation of alkylenebismelamine derivatives usable as components for forming resin materials including aminoplasts, and flame-retardant materials. Specifically, a process for the preparation of alkylenebismelamines wherein the alkylene is a C2-C10 linear or branched one by reacting an alkylenediamine wherein the alkylene is a C2-C10 linear or branched one with melamine under heating in the presence of an acidic catalyst, characterized in that the amount of melamine is at least twice that of the alkylenediamine by mole.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce procédé permet de préparer facilement et à bas coût des dérivés d'alkylènebismélamine, utiles en tant que constituants servant à former des matières résineuses, notamment des aminoplastes et des matières ignifuges. L'invention concerne plus particulièrement un procédé de préparation d'alkylènebismélamines, consistant à obtenir un alkylène linéaire ou ramifié en C2-C10, en faisant réagir une alkylènediamine, dans laquelle l'alkylène est un alkylène, linéaire ou ramifié, en C2-C10, avec une mélamine, sous chauffage et en présence d'un catalyseur acide, ce procédé étant caractérisé en ce que la quantité molaire de mélamine est au moins deux fois celle de l'alkylènediamine.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>